C*******************************************************************************
C
C                          IWFM DEMAND CALCULATOR (IDC)
C                              *** Version 2.1 ***
C
C*******************************************************************************
C
C                          RETURN FLOW FRACTION DATA FILE 
C
C
C             Project :  CALSIM 3.0 Development                         
C             Filename:   ReturnFlowFactor.dat                        
C
C*******************************************************************************
C                              File Description
C
C   This data file contains a set of time series data for initial return flow as a 
C   fraction of applied water.  The net return flow is computed as the initial return 
C   flow less the re-used portion of the initial return flow. Individual time-series 
C   data columns are associted with each subregion and crop combination in the 
C   Parameter Data File.
C
C*******************************************************************************
C                   Return Flow Fraction Data Specifications
C
C   NRF    ;  Number of initial return flow fraction data columns
C   DSSFL  ;  The name of the DSS file for data input (maximum 100 characters); 
C              * Leave blank if DSS file is not used for data input
C
C-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
C         VALUE                     DESCRIPTION
C-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
             3                       / NRF
                                    / DSSFL
C-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
C                          Return Flow Fractions
C                          (READ FROM THIS FILE)
C
C   List the initial return flow fractions below, if it will not be read from
C   a DSS file (i.e. DSSFL is left blank above).
C
C   ITRF ;   Time
C   RF   ;   Return flow fraction. It is defined as the ratio of the  
C            return flow to the applied water; [dimensionless]
C		For urban, this is only applicable to outdoor return flow	
C            
C-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
C ITRF     RF[1]  RF[2]  RF[3] ..... RF[NRF]
C-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
10/31/4000_24:00   	0.1	 1.0  	 0.0
11/30/4000_24:00   	0.1	 1.0  	 0.0
12/31/4000_24:00   	0.1	 1.0  	 0.0
01/31/4000_24:00   	0.1	 1.0  	 0.0
02/29/4000_24:00   	0.1	 1.0  	 0.0
03/31/4000_24:00   	0.1	 1.0  	 0.0
04/30/4000_24:00   	0.1	 1.0  	 0.0
05/31/4000_24:00   	0.1	 1.0  	 0.0
06/30/4000_24:00   	0.1	 1.0     0.0
07/31/4000_24:00   	0.1	 1.0  	 0.0
08/31/4000_24:00   	0.1	 1.0  	 0.0
09/30/4000_24:00   	0.1	 1.0  	 0.0
C			AG     all to	 all to
C			       surface	  DP
C-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
C                         Pathnames for Return Flow Fractions
C                               (READ FROM DSS FILE)
C
C   List the pathnames for initial return flow fractions below, if it will be read
C   from a DSS file (i.e. DSSFL is specified above).
C
C   REC  ;  Time series record number
C   PATH ;  Pathname for the time series record 
C
C-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
C   REC       PATH
